│ Okay, let’s proceed. I’ve analyzed the code  │
│ retrieved via get_code_around_line and the   │
│ search_method_in_class call. The core issue  │
│ is that YearInSchool is a class that’s being │
│ treated as callable in Django templates,     │
│ leading to errors. The solution is to        │
│ explicitly prevent it from being called in   │
│ templates.                                   │
│                                              │
│ Reasoning:                                   │
│                                              │
│ The __call__ method in YearInSchool is what  │
│ allows instances of the class to be called   │
│ like functions. Django templates, however,   │
│ treat calls to objects as function calls,    │
│ which is why it fails when trying to compare │
│ against YearInSchool.FRESHMAN.  Adding       │
│ do_not_call_in_templates = True to the class │
│ definition will prevent this behavior in     │
│ templates.                                   │
│                                              │
│ Patch:                                       │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  # modification 1                            │
│  [file]models.py[/file]                      │
│  [original]                                  │
│  class YearInSchool(Enum):                   │
│      FRESHMAN = 1                            │
│      SOPHOMORE = 2                           │
│      JUNIOR = 3                              │
│      SENIOR = 4                              │
│                                              │
│      def __str__(self):                      │
│          return self.name                    │
│  [/original]                                 │
